<h4 id="gopher-link-support">Gopher link support</h4>
<p></p>
<p>The <em>gopher</em> link support requires user to add something like this to
their user config:</p>
<pre><code class="language-emacs-lisp">(with-eval-after-load 'org
  (defun org-link-gopher-export-link (link desc format)
    "Create export version of LINK and DESC to FORMAT."
    (let ((link (concat "gopher:" link)))
      (cond
       ((eq format 'html)
        (format "&#x3C;a href=\"%s\">%s&#x3C;/a>" link desc))
       ((eq format 'latex)
        (format "\\href{%s}{%s}" link desc))
       (t                               ;`ascii', `md', `hugo', etc.
        (format "[%s](%s)" desc link)))))
  (org-link-set-parameters "gopher" :export #'org-link-gopher-export-link))
</code></pre>
<p>Once that is evaluated, links like these will export fine i.e. no
“Unable to resolve link” errors:</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">[[gopher://some.gopher.site][Dummy gopher link]]
</code></pre>
