<h3 id="org-cite">Org Cite</h3>
<h4 id="org-cite-basic-example">Org Cite Basic Example</h4>
<p><strong>Org 9.5</strong> is needed for this as that version introduced</p>
<div class="mark">
<p>the new <strong>oc.el</strong> Org Cite library</p>
</div>
<p>.</p>
<h5 id="specify-bibligraphy-files">Specify Bibligraphy files</h5>
<p>Org Cite (<code>oc.el</code>) requires the bibliography files to be specified
using one or more <code>#+bibliography: &#x3C;file.bib></code> keywords or using the
<code>org-cite-global-bibliography</code> variable.</p>
<p>Example: <code>#+bibliography: orgcite.bib</code></p>
<div class="theorem" data-kind="note">
<p><span class="theorem-head"><span class="theorem-name">Note</span>.</span> <code>:EXPORT_BIBLIOGRAPHY:</code> in subtree property drawers will <strong>not</strong> work
with Org Cite!</p>
</div>
<h5 id="citation-syntax">Citation Syntax</h5>
<p>Below Org snippet:</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">[cite:@OrgCitations]
</code></pre>
<p>exports to:</p>
<p></p>
<p>See <a href="https://blog.tecosaur.com/tmio/2021-07-31-citations.html">the <em>TMIO</em> July 2021 blog post</a> for more information on the <code>cite:</code>
syntax.</p>
<h5 id="printing-bibliography">Printing Bibliography</h5>
<p>Below Org snippet:</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">#+print_bibliography:
</code></pre>
<p>exports to:</p>
