<h4 id="citation-forms">Citation Forms</h4>
<h5 id="citation-forms-test-body">Citation Forms Test Body</h5>
<h6 id="citations-in-square-brackets">Citations in square brackets</h6>
<p>The citations withing square brackets will be rendered within
parentheses.</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">Blah blah [see @doe99, pp. 33-35; also @smith04, ch. 1].
</code></pre>
<p>Blah blah [see @doe99, pp. 33-35; also @smith04, ch. 1].</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">Blah blah [@doe99, pp. 33-35, 38-39].
</code></pre>
<p>Blah blah [@doe99, pp. 33-35, 38-39].</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">Blah blah [@smith04; @doe99].
</code></pre>
<p>Blah blah [@smith04; @doe99].</p>
<h6 id="citations-with-author-name-suppressed">Citations with author name suppressed</h6>
<p>A minus sign (<code>-</code>) before the <code>@</code> will suppress mention of the author
in the citation. This can be useful when the author is already
mentioned in the text.</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">Smith says blah [-@smith04].
</code></pre>
<p>Smith says blah [-@smith04].</p>
<h6 id="in-text-citations-no-square-brackets">In-text citations (no square brackets)</h6>
<pre><code class="language-org">@smith04 says blah.
</code></pre>
<p>@smith04 says blah.</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">@smith04 [p. 33] says blah.
</code></pre>
<p>@smith04 [p. 33] says blah.</p>
<h6 id="actual-citations-for-this-test-post">Actual citations for this test post :)</h6>
<p>See @addCite17; @rmdCitations for more.</p>
