<h4 id="export-snippet-markdown">Export snippet Markdown</h4>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<dl>
<dt>NOTE</dt>
<dd><code>ox-md.el</code> does not support <strong>Export Snippets</strong> as of writing
this <span class="timestamp-wrapper"><time class="timestamp" datetime="2017-12-08">&#x3C;2017-12-08 Fri></time></span>. So even the <code>@@md:foo@@</code> and
<code>@@markdown:foo@@</code> snippets are handled by <code>ox-hugo</code>
directly.</dd>
</dl>
<h4 id="export-snippet-html">Export snippet HTML</h4>
<p>This HTML <b>Export Snippet</b> will also get exported for Hugo
exports, <code>verbatim</code>.</p>
<h3 id="export-block">Export block</h3>
<h4 id="export-block-hugo">Export block Hugo</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Testing <code>#+begin_export hugo</code> .. <code>#+end_export</code> blocks.</p>
</div>
<h5 id="using-export-hugo-block-for-unpaired-shortcodes-with-named-arguments">Using <em>export hugo</em> block for unpaired shortcodes with named arguments</h5>
<p>Below:</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">#+begin_export hugo
{{&#x3C; myshortcode-named
      arg1="horizontal"
      arg2="static/img/legacy/works/land"
>}}
#+end_export
</code></pre>
<p>renders as:</p>
<h4 id="export-block-markdown">Export block Markdown</h4>
<h4 id="export-block-html">Export block HTML</h4>
This HTML <b>Export Block</b>  will also get exported for Hugo exports,
<code>verbatim</code>.

And Markdown emphasis characters like *, `  and _ will not escaped in here.
<p>From , we see an actual case of where that <code>*</code>
will need to remain unescaped:</p>
<pre><code class="language-org"># Org source
#+begin_export html
&#x3C;div>
  &#x3C;script type="text/javascript">
    var a = 3;
    var b = 2*a;
  &#x3C;/script>
&#x3C;/div>
#+end_export
</code></pre>
<div>
  <script type="text/javascript">
    var a = 3;
    var b = 2*a;
  </script>
</div>
<h5 id="begin_export-html-blocks-with-script-tag"><code>#+begin_export html</code> blocks with script tag</h5>
<p></p>
<p>Check that <code>src="https://example.com"</code> does not become
<code>src="&#x3C;https://example.com>"</code>.</p>
<dl>
<dt>Note</dt>
<dd>Below iframe/script will <strong>not</strong> work on this site because of
the strict <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CSP">CSP</a>. Anyways. this site is to test just the
Markdown exported by ox-hugo. So please see ”<em>✱ Markdown
source of this page</em>” above.</dd>
</dl>
<pre><code class="language-org">#+begin_export html
&#x3C;div class="glitch-embed-wrap" style="height: 420px; width: 100%;">
  &#x3C;iframe
    src="https://glitch.com/embed/#!/embed/silken-football?path=app.py&#x26;previewSize=0&#x26;sidebarCollapsed=true"
    title="silken-football on Glitch"
    style="height: 100%; width: 100%; border: 0;">
  &#x3C;/iframe>
&#x3C;/div>
#+end_export
</code></pre>
<div class="glitch-embed-wrap" style="height: 420px; width: 100%;">
  <iframe
    src="https://glitch.com/embed/#!/embed/silken-football?path=app.py&previewSize=0&sidebarCollapsed=true"
    title="silken-football on Glitch"
    style="height: 100%; width: 100%; border: 0;">
  </iframe>
</div>
<h5 id="to-see-the-exported-html">To see the exported HTML</h5>
<p><em>See the Markdown source of this page to see the verbatim-inserted
HTML.</em></p>
<h2 id="miscellaneous-front-matter">Miscellaneous Front Matter</h2>
<h3 id="hugo-aliases">Hugo Aliases</h3>
<h4 id="alias-without-section-portion-1">Alias without section portion 1</h4>
<p>As the specified alias does not contain the ”/” string, it will be
auto-prefixed with the section for the current post.</p>
<h4 id="new-section-just-for-test">New section just for test</h4>
<h5 id="alias-without-section-portion-2">Alias without section portion 2</h5>
<p>As the specified alias does not contain the ”/” string, it will be
auto-prefixed with the section for the current post.</p>
<h4 id="alias-specifying-a-different-section">Alias specifying a different section</h4>
<h4 id="alias-specifying-root-section">Alias specifying root section</h4>
<h4 id="multiple-aliases-without-section-portion">Multiple aliases without section portion</h4>
<h4 id="multiple-aliases-with-section-portion">Multiple aliases with section portion</h4>
<h3 id="author">Author</h3>
<h4 id="single-author-parent-subtree">Single author parent subtree</h4>
<h5 id="single-author">Single author</h5>
<p>This post has 1 author set as a TOML list in front-matter.</p>
<h4 id="single-author-as-a-custom-parameter">Single author as a custom parameter</h4>
<p>This post has 1 author set as a TOML string in front-matter.</p>
<h4 id="multiple-authors">Multiple authors</h4>
<p>This post has multiple authors. In Org, multiple authors are added
comma-separated.</p>
<h4 id="uniquify-duplicate-authors">Uniquify duplicate authors</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Test that duplicate authors get uniquified in the export.</p>
</div>
<p>The duplication can happen in real use if an Org setup file has the
same author as in the Org document where that file is included using
<code>SETUPFILE</code>. This test mimics this case:</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">#+setupfile: some-file.org # some-file.org contains "#+author: Foo Bar"
#+author: Foo Bar
</code></pre>
<h3 id="keywords-1">Keywords</h3>
<h4 id="single-keyword-in-front-matter">Single keyword in front-matter</h4>
<h4 id="multiple-keywords-in-front-matter">Multiple keywords in front-matter</h4>
<h4 id="keywords-set-using-multiple-properties">Keywords set using multiple properties</h4>
<h3 id="description">Description</h3>
<h4 id="description-meta-data-with-quoted-text">Description meta-data with “quoted text”</h4>
<p>Testing a post with double quotes in the description.</p>
<h4 id="description-set-using-org-special-block">Description set using Org Special Block</h4>
<h5 id="toml-1">TOML</h5>
<h6 id="single-line-description-set-using-org-special-block-toml">Single-line description set using Org Special Block (TOML)</h6>
<div class="description">
<p>Short description — <strong>bold</strong> – <em>italics</em> — <del>strikethrough</del> <code>monospace</code></p>
</div>
<p>Post content.</p>
<h6 id="multi-line-description-set-using-org-special-block-toml">Multi-line description set using Org Special Block (TOML)</h6>
<div class="description">
<p>Short description
of this post</p>
<p><strong>bold</strong> – <em>italics</em> — <del>strikethrough</del> <code>monospace</code></p>
<p>These lines <br>
show up with line breaks <br>
but within the same paragraph.</p>
</div>
<p>Post content.</p>
<h6 id="special-block-description-overrides-property-set-description">Special block description overrides property-set description</h6>
<p>If the description is set via the subtree property
<code>:EXPORT_DESCRIPTION</code> (or the <code>#+description</code> keyword), and via the
“description” special block too, the latter will take precedence.</p>
<div class="description">
<p>Description set in special block</p>
</div>
