<h3 id="locale">Locale</h3>
<h4 id="specified-locale-in-front-matter">Specified locale in front-matter</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Specify the locale using <code>:EXPORT_HUGO_LOCALE: es_ES</code> property.</p>
</div>
<p>Locale exporting is enabled using <code>:EXPORT_HUGO_WITH_LOCALE: t</code> in the
post’s parent subtree.</p>
<h4 id="auto-detected-locale-in-front-matter">Auto-detected locale in front-matter</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Locale is not specified, so is auto-detected.</p>
</div>
<p>Locale exporting is enabled using <code>:EXPORT_HUGO_WITH_LOCALE: t</code> in the
post’s parent subtree.</p>
<h3 id="images">Images</h3>
<h4 id="single-image">Single image</h4>
<p>If an image path has spaces in it, wrap the whole path in double
quotes.</p>
<h4 id="multiple-images">Multiple images</h4>
<p>If an image path has spaces in it, wrap the whole path in double
quotes.</p>
<h3 id="videos">Videos</h3>
<h4 id="single-video">Single video</h4>
<p>If a video path has spaces in it, wrap the whole path in double
quotes.</p>
<h4 id="multiple-videos">Multiple videos</h4>
<p>If a video path has spaces in it, wrap the whole path in double
quotes.</p>
<h3 id="audio">Audio</h3>
<p>If the audio path has spaces in it, wrap the whole path in double
quotes.</p>
<h3 id="series">Series</h3>
<h4 id="single-series">Single series</h4>
<p>If a series name has spaces in it, wrap the whole name in double
quotes.</p>
<h4 id="multiple-series">Multiple series</h4>
<p>If a series name has spaces in it, wrap the whole name in double
quotes.</p>
<h3 id="type">Type</h3>
<h4 id="type-front-matter">Type Front-matter</h4>
<p>The <code>type</code> front-matter is used to override the default <strong>section</strong> type
(automatically derived from the directory of the content page).</p>
<p>Here the type is overridden to be <code>type-test</code>.</p>
<p><a href="https://gohugo.io/content-management/front-matter/#predefined">Reference</a></p>
<h4 id="type--layout-front-matter">Type + Layout Front-matter</h4>
<p>Here both <code>type</code> <strong>and</strong> <code>layout</code> are overridden.</p>
<h3 id="layout-front-matter">Layout Front-matter</h3>
<p>The <code>layout</code> front-matter is used to override the default <strong>single</strong>
layout of a regular page. See <a href="https://gohugo.io/templates/lookup-order/">Template Lookup Order</a> to learn more.</p>
<p>Here the layout is overridden to be <code>alternate-single</code>.</p>
<p><a href="https://gohugo.io/content-management/front-matter/#predefined">Reference</a></p>
<h3 id="url-front-matter">URL Front-matter</h3>
<p>The <code>url</code> front-matter is used to specify <strong>the full path to the
content from the web root</strong>. It makes no assumptions about the path of
the content file. It also ignores any language prefixes of the
multilingual feature.</p>
<p><a href="https://gohugo.io/content-management/front-matter/#predefined">Reference</a></p>
<h3 id="linktitle-front-matter">Linktitle Front-matter</h3>
<p>The <code>linktitle</code> front-matter is used for creating links to content. If
set, Hugo defaults to using the <code>linktitle</code> before the <code>title</code>.</p>
<h3 id="slug-front-matter">Slug Front-matter</h3>
<p>By default, a page’s <em>slug</em> is the name of the content file (sans
extension). So in this case, it would have been
<code>slug-front-matter</code>. But that slug is overridden using the specified
<code>slug</code> in the front-matter: <code>this-is-how-i-want-to-name-this-link</code>.</p>
<h3 id="markup-front-matter">Markup Front-matter</h3>
<p>The markup for this post is set to <code>org</code>. So the Markdown markup based
emphasis <strong>won’t work</strong> here.</p>
<h3 id="replace-front-matter-keys">Replace front-matter keys</h3>
<h4 id="replace-description-with-summary">Replace “description” with “summary”</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>This should be rendered as <code>.Summary</code> in Hugo v0.55+. For only Hugo
versions, this will front-matter can be retrieved only as
<code>.Params.summary</code>.</p>
</div>
<p>This text will be in the post body.</p>
<h4 id="replace-only-linktitle-key">Replace only “linkTitle” key</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>linkTitle</code> key in front-matter replaced with
<code>linktitle</code>.</p>
<h4 id="replace-only-tags-key">Replace only “tags” key</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>tags</code> key in front-matter replaced with
<code>keywords</code>.</p>
<h4 id="replace-only-categories-key">Replace only “categories” key</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>categories</code> key in front-matter replaced with
<code>cats</code>.</p>
<h4 id="replace-both-tags-and-categories-keys">Replace both “tags” and “categories” keys</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>tags</code> key in front-matter replaced with
<code>keywords</code> and <code>categories</code> replaced with <code>cats</code>.</p>
<h4 id="replace-keys-using-multiple-properties">Replace keys using multiple properties</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>tags</code> key in front-matter replaced with
<code>keywords</code> and <code>categories</code> replaced with <code>cats</code>.</p>
<h4 id="swap-tags-and-categories">Swap tags and categories</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>tags</code> and <code>categories</code> keys in the
front-matter swapped.</p>
<h4 id="replace-custom-keys">Replace custom keys</h4>
<p>This post will have the <code>foo</code> key in front-matter replaced with
<code>myfoo</code> and <code>bar</code> replaced with <code>mybar</code>.</p>
<h4 id="attempt-to-replace-non-existing-keys">Attempt to replace non-existing keys</h4>
<p>Here, attempt is made to replace a non-existing key <code>toto</code>, but still,
there shouldn’t be any error.</p>
<h4 id="make-the-author-front-matter-plural">Make the author front-matter plural</h4>
<p>Some themes might expect the front-matter list variable for authors to
be <code>authors</code> instead of the default <code>author</code> created by <code>ox-hugo</code>.</p>
<h4 id="remove-a-front-matter-key">Remove a front-matter key</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>This test removes the <code>foo</code> front-matter key from the exported file
(and replaces <code>bar</code> key with <code>zoo</code>).</p>
</div>
<h3 id="logbook-notes">LOGBOOK Notes</h3>
<h4 id="parsing-notes-from-logbook">Parsing notes from LOGBOOK</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Parse notes from LOGBOOK into a TOML table (YAML map?) of
<code>logbook.notes</code> front-matter.</p>
</div>
<p></p>
<p>For example,</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">:LOGBOOK:
- Note taken on [2018-09-06 Thu 11:45] \\
  Another note.
- Note taken on [2018-09-06 Thu 11:37] \\
  A note
- State "DONE"       from "DRAFT"      [2018-09-06 Thu 11:25]
- State "DRAFT"      from "TODO"       [2018-09-06 Thu 11:25]
- State "TODO"       from              [2018-09-06 Thu 11:25]
:END:
</code></pre>
<p>should export only the notes to an array of TOML tables with key
<code>logbook.&#x3C;..>.notes</code>. The notes are ordered starting from the newest
note first in the TOML table array to the oldest note at the last.</p>
<dl>
<dt>Note</dt>
<dd>The state change notes are intentionally put in this test
LOGBOOK, because we want to ensure that they don’t seep into the
<code>logbook.&#x3C;..>.notes</code> front-matter.</dd>
</dl>
<h4 id="logbook-notes-in-nested-headings">LOGBOOK Notes in nested headings</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Parse notes from LOGBOOK drawers in top-level and nested headings.</p>
</div>
<h5 id="sub-heading">Sub-heading</h5>
<h5 id="sub-heading-with-markup">Sub heading <strong>with</strong> <em>markup</em></h5>
<p>Some text in body between two <code>:LOGBOOK:</code> drawers.</p>
<p>Text after the second <code>:LOGBOOK:</code> drawer.</p>
<h4 id="post-marked-as-done-with-logbook-notes-in-nested-headings">Post marked as DONE with LOGBOOK Notes in nested headings</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Parse notes from LOGBOOK drawers in top-level and nested headings.</p>
</div>
<p>The <code>lastmod</code> field is not set for this post (even if it has a note
with timestamp) because this post is not marked as DONE.</p>
<h5 id="sub-heading-2">Sub-heading</h5>
<h4 id="parse-lastmod-from-logbook-notes-with-no-recorded-state-changes">Parse lastmod from LOGBOOK Notes with no recorded state changes</h4>
<div class="description">
<p>Parse <code>lastmod</code> from toplevel LOGBOOK notes even if the drawer didn’t
record any state changes.</p>
</div>
<h3 id="extra-front-matter-tests">Extra Front-matter tests</h3>
<h4 id="extra-front-matter">Extra Front-matter</h4>
<h5 id="toml-front-matter">TOML Front-matter</h5>
<h6 id="extra-front-matter-toml-toml-extra">Extra Front-matter (TOML, TOML extra)</h6>
<p></p>
<p>The <code>#+begin_src toml :front_matter_extra t</code> TOML block here will get
appended to the TOML front-matter.</p>
<pre><code class="language-toml"># List your qualifications (such as academic degrees).
[[education.courses]]
  course = "PhD in Artificial Intelligence"
  institution = "Stanford University"
  year = 2012

[[education.courses]]
  course = "MEng in Artificial Intelligence"
  institution = "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"
  year = 2009

[[education.courses]]
  course = "BSc in Artificial Intelligence"
  institution = "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"
  year = 2008
</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-toml"># this TOML block will export to the Markdown body
</code></pre>
<h6 id="extra-front-matter-toml-yaml-extra">Extra Front-matter (TOML, YAML extra)</h6>
<p></p>
<p>The <code>#+begin_src yaml :front_matter_extra t</code> YAML block here will get
discarded because the front-matter type is TOML.</p>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">education:
  courses:
    - course: PhD in Artificial Intelligence
      institution: Stanford University
      year: 2012
    - course: MEng in Artificial Intelligence
      institution: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
      year: 2009
    - course: BSc in Artificial Intelligence
      institution: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
      year: 2008
</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-toml"># this TOML block will export to the Markdown body
</code></pre>
